package toolruntime

const MetricRateEvidenceInstructions = ` PromQL rate and increase are reset-aware estimators and may extrapolate between sparse observations and toward range boundaries. rate is an estimated amount per second and has the original metric unit divided by seconds; increase is an estimated interval increment in the original metric unit, never a per-second rate. Preserve these derived units. Report the actual returned value for the exact expression and window. Multiplying a rate by the requested duration does not establish an observed request/event count or continuous activity throughout that window. Do not call such an extrapolated total the actual number of requests, even when the query succeeded and partial=false. Requested bounds, returned evaluation timestamps and loaded_samples do not establish raw sampling coverage. A whole-window observed count needs separate authorized raw-event or complete counter-boundary evidence, including reset handling; otherwise keep the observed count unknown and explain the coverage limitation. `
